    {
      "id": "bf1f554b3858-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "If \\(\\rm \\frac{\\cosθ}{(1+\\sinθ)}+\\frac{\\cosθ}{(1-\\sinθ)}\\) = 4 and &theta; is acute, then the value of &theta; is :",
      "questionHtml": "If&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\rm \\frac{\\cosθ}{(1+\\sinθ)}+\\frac{\\cosθ}{(1-\\sinθ)}\\)</span>= 4 and&nbsp;&theta; is acute, then the value of&nbsp;&theta; is :",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "60&deg;",
          "html": "60&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "15&deg;",
          "html": "15&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "45&deg;",
          "html": "45&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "30&deg;",
          "html": "30&deg;&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>[cosθ(1 - sinθ) + <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">cos</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">θ(1 + sinθ)]/[(1 - sinθ).(1 + sin</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">θ)] = 4 ⇒ [cosθ - cosθsinθ + </span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">cosθ + cos</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">θ sinθ]/(1 - sin<sup>2</sup>θ) = 4</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ 2cosθ</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">/cos<span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>θ = 4 ⇒ cosθ= 1/2 = cos 60°</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bf1f554b3858-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "In a triangle ABC, &ang;A = 2&theta;, &ang; B = &ang; C = 4 &theta; and &theta; satisfies 4 sin 2 &theta; + 2 sin &theta; - 1 = 0. What is the ratio of BC to AB?",
      "questionHtml": "In a triangle ABC, &ang;A = 2&theta;, <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>B = <span style=\"\">&ang;</span>C = 4<span style=\"\">&theta;</span> and <span style=\"\">&theta;</span> satisfies 4 sin<sup>2</sup><span style=\"\">&theta;</span> + 2 sin <span style=\"\">&theta;</span> - 1 = 0. What is the ratio of BC to AB?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "&radic;5 - 1",
          "html": "&radic;5 - 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{2}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{2}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{4}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{4}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "2(&radic;5 - 1)",
          "html": "2(&radic;5 - 1)"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In a triangle ABC, &ang;A = 2&theta;,&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ang;</span><span style=\"\">B =&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ang;</span><span style=\"\">C = 4</span><span style=\"\">&theta;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&theta;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;satisfies 4 sin</span><span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"\">&theta;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;+ 2 sin&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&theta;</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;- 1 = 0.</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Concept used:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Isosceles triangle:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p>The altitude from vertex A to the base BC is the perpendicular bisector of the base BC.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Quadratic formula</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\({-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2-4ac} \\over 2a}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>sin &theta; =&nbsp;Perpendicular / Hypotenuse</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">4sin<span style=\"line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em; font-size:10.5px;\">2</span>&theta;&nbsp;+ 2sin&nbsp;&theta;&nbsp;- 1 = 0</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; sin&theta; =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {-2 \\pm \\sqrt{2^2-4\\times (-1) \\times (4)} \\over 8}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; sin&theta; =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {-2 \\pm 2\\sqrt{5} \\over 8}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; sin&theta; =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {-2 + 2\\sqrt{5} \\over 8}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; sin&theta; =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {\\sqrt{5} - 1 \\over 4}\\)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ----(1)</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F2_Madhuri_Defence_26.09.2022_D3.png\" style=\"height: 293px; width: 266px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In&nbsp;&Delta;ABD,</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; sin&theta; =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{BD}{AB}\\)</span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;(sin &theta; = P/H)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Using equation (1)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{b}{{a}}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {\\sqrt{5} - 1 \\over 4}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;-----(2)</span></p>\n\n<p>Now, in&nbsp;&Delta; ABD</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{BC}{{AB}}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{2b}{{a}}\\)</span>&nbsp;=&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(2\\times \\frac{b}{{a}}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr; <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{BC}{{AB}}\\)</span>&nbsp;= (2&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\( {\\sqrt{5} - 1 \\over 4}\\)</span>)&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;[From equation (2)]</p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{BC}{{AB}}\\)</span>&nbsp;=<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{2}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The required value is&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{(\\sqrt5-1)}{2}\\)</span></strong>.</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F2_Madhuri_Defence_26.09.2022_D3.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bf1f554b3858-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "If cos A = \\(\\frac{1}{11}\\) , then find the value of cot A.",
      "questionHtml": "If cos A =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{11}\\)</span>, then find the value of cot A.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{2\\sqrt 30}{11}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{2\\sqrt 30}{11}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "2&radic;30",
          "html": "2&radic;30"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt 30}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt 30}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{11}{2\\sqrt 30}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{11}{2\\sqrt 30}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>First, let's use the Pythagorean identity for sine and cosine to figure out sin A:</p>\n\n<p>sin<sup>2</sup> A + cos<sup>2</sup> A = 1 ⇒ sin<sup>2</sup> A = 1 - (1/11)<sup>2 </sup>⇒ <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">sin</span><span style=\"position: relative;  line-height: 0; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">​</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"> A</span><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"> </span>= 120/121 ⇒ sin A = √(120/121)</p>\n\n<p>Since cot A = cos A / sin A:</p>\n\n<p>⇒ cot A = (1/11) /<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"> √(120/121) </span>⇒ <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">cot A = 1/</span>√120 = <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt 30}\\)</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bf1f554b3858-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "If \\(1 + tan θ = \\sqrt3, then, \\sqrt3 cot θ - 1\\) = ?",
      "questionHtml": "If&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(1 + tan θ = \\sqrt3, then, \\sqrt3 cot θ - 1\\)</span> = ?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\((\\sqrt3 \\space+\\space 1)/(2)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\sqrt3 \\space+\\space 1)/(2)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\((2\\sqrt3 \\space-\\space 1)/(2)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((2\\sqrt3 \\space-\\space 1)/(2)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\((2\\sqrt3 \\space+\\space 1)/(2)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((2\\sqrt3 \\space+\\space 1)/(2)\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\((\\sqrt3 \\space-\\space 1)/(2)\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\sqrt3 \\space-\\space 1)/(2)\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((1 + \\tan \\theta = \\sqrt{3})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula used:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\tan \\theta = \\dfrac{\\sin \\theta}{\\cos \\theta})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{\\tan \\theta})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((1 + \\tan \\theta = \\sqrt{3})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((⇒ \\tan \\theta = \\sqrt{3} - 1)\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{\\tan \\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - 1})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>Rationalize the denominator:</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} × \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{(\\sqrt{3})^2 - 1^2})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(⇒ \\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{3 - 1} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{2}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>Now, <span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\sqrt{3} \\cot \\theta - 1)\\)</span>:</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\sqrt{3} \\cot \\theta - 1 = \\sqrt{3} × \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} + 1}{2} - 1)\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(⇒ (\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3} × \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{3}}{2} - 1)\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(⇒ (\\dfrac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2} - 1)\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(⇒ (\\dfrac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2} - \\dfrac{2}{2})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\dfrac{3 + \\sqrt{3} - 2}{2})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p>&rArr;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{3}}{2})\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\((\\sqrt{3} \\cot \\theta - 1 = \\dfrac{1 + \\sqrt{3}}{2})\\)</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bf1f554b3858-q5",
